# Preserve upstream code style

- For all development in this fork, follow the original author's style in the
  surrounding upstream code: indentation, spacing, naming, braces, quotes,
  semicolons, imports, comments, and component/module organization.
- Read the relevant existing files before editing or adding code. For new files,
  follow the closest comparable upstream file's conventions.
- Keep changes focused. Do not reformat unrelated code or replace established
  patterns with personal preferences; avoid broad formatter-driven changes.
- Follow the original app's interface style for all UI work. Reuse its existing
  components, button classes, colors, typography, spacing, and icon conventions.
  Match the original primary/secondary action styling rather than introducing a
  separate appearance for new controls.
- Keep this instruction in project guidance, outside the feature/fix backlog.
